Package: splineKANr
Type: Package
Title: B-Spline Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks in Native R 'torch'
Version: 0.5.1
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Thang", family = "Le-Dinh",
           email = "thang87sg@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Implements Kolmogorov-Arnold Networks (KAN) whose edge
    functions are B-splines plus a residual base activation, written in
    native R on top of the 'torch' package. Provides Cox-de Boor basis
    evaluation with explicit extrapolation policies, multi-layer networks,
    Adam and L-BFGS training with validation, early stopping, input and
    output normalization, gradient clipping and reproducible seeds,
    adaptive (sample-based) grid updates, grid refinement, KAN-specific
    sparsity regularization, pruning, edge-function visualization and
    model persistence. A dependency-free base R reference implementation
    with analytic gradients is included as a numerical oracle and as a
    training backend that does not need 'libtorch'. The design follows
    Liu et al. (2024) <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2404.19756>.
